VERDICT: APPROVED_WITH_COMMENTS

The project is functionally set up: the Flask app serves the UI, configured workflow and autoscale Gunicorn deployment target are present, and smoke tests passed for the page, overview, valid/invalid predictions, and custom-classification validation/rule path.

The only material follow-up is that `cached_stock_info()` is implemented but `/api/predict` calls `stock_data.get_stock_info()` directly. Thus every prediction performs a synchronous Yahoo Finance request rather than using the intended five-minute cache, which can unnecessarily increase latency and provider load. Wire the route to the cache helper (or remove the unused helper) before expanding usage.

Security: no serious issue observed. The SAST finding is for VERDICT: APPROVED_WITH_COMMENTS
Flask binding to all interfaces, but debug is disabled and production uses Gunicorn; this is appropriate for the configured container deployment.

Next action: connect `/api/predict` to `cached_stock_info()` and perform a deployed smoke test with the opti
onal OpenAI secret configured if custom LLM classification is intended.

